Adaptations:
- Independent port66 source set; native 6.6 implementations retain their original semantics.
- Module-owned PID/IPC namespaces, IPC task side table, proc/sysctl/mqueue registration.
- Selected fork/exit/PID/proc/namespace functions replace native entries in matching QEMU only.
- IPC syscall slots, reboot and memfd policy wrappers; BPF callback pointers and FUSE/cgroup refs.
- Perf uses the native implementation with checked prologue trampolines and owned PID refs.
- No pidfs namespace ioctl hook: this interface is not present in the 6.6 baseline.
- Native 6.6 FUSE initialization retained; PID reference dropped in delayed_release
  because native fuse_conn_put is inlined into fuse_dev_free/fuse_mount_destroy.
- 6.6 vendor exit hook declaration and mutable ctl_table handler signatures retained.
- SHM_HUGETLB is rejected: CONFIG_SYSVIPC=n native MM uses a false inline SHM hugepage predicate.
- PLC110 6.6.118 boot image adds a second QEMU target; see docs/plc110-6.6-vm.md.
- proc_exit_connector is resolved dynamically because CONFIG_PROC_EVENTS differs.
- Explicit plc110_test=1 permits device testing on the exact PLC110 6.6.118 release.
  The manual loader verifies Android model, kernel BTF and payload checksum.
- No automatic boot package or release promotion for this experimental build.
